# Niagara Tools

These tools are local UnrealMCP Niagara extensions for inspection and limited authoring. Most mutating asset operations route to the C++ bridge; offline temp cleanup is Python-only and does not load editor assets.

Use Python/editor scripting for asset duplication, preview capture, and broad orchestration. Use these C++ tools only for Niagara APIs that are unsafe, protected, or impractical through Unreal Python.

## Tools

- `analyze_niagara_system(system_path, include_renderers=true, include_user_parameters=true, include_stack=true, include_graph=true, include_module_inputs=true, include_compile_status=true, include_pins=false, include_links=false, include_scratch_pads=true, include_resolved_stack_inputs=false, max_function_calls=200, max_nodes_per_graph=300, max_links_per_graph=0, max_modules=200, max_candidates_per_module=24, max_resolved_inputs_per_module=8, max_top_candidates=80)`
  - Aggregates the existing read-only renderer, User parameter, stack, graph, module input, and compile-health inspections into one response.
  - Does not save, request compile, or mutate source assets.
  - Returns `summary`, `section_status`, `limitations`, and the included section payloads.
- `inspect_niagara_factory_bootstrap_defaults(kind="all", create_default_system_nodes=true, add_default_modules_and_renderers=false, include_pins=false, max_function_calls=80)`
  - Creates transient `UNiagaraSystem` and/or `UNiagaraEmitter` objects with UE's Niagara factories and reports the default scripts, graph nodes, function calls, output nodes, renderer defaults, and emitter properties.
  - `kind` may be `all`, `system`, `emitter`, `empty_emitter`, or `basic_sprite_emitter`.
  - This is read-only and transient-only: it does not create a package, register an asset, save, or request compile.
- `audit_niagara_promotion_candidate(system_path, proposed_target_path="", forbidden_dependency_prefixes=None, forbidden_source_roots=None, allow_temp_target=false, allow_temp_dependencies=false, timeout_seconds=60.0)`
  - Read-only preflight for moving a generated Niagara System out of `/Game/_MCP_Temp`.
  - Loads the candidate, scans its saved package file when available, and returns exact package dependency hits for MCP/plugin references and `/Game/_MCP_Temp` references.
  - `proposed_target_path` is optional, but when provided it must be a valid non-temp `/Game` package path unless `allow_temp_target=true`.
  - Use `forbidden_source_roots` when a promoted copy must not retain dependencies on a source/template content root.
  - This command does not duplicate, move, save, compile, or delete assets; it only reports `promotion_ready` and `promotion_blockers`.
  - `promotion_ready` also requires a complete Asset Registry dependency query and saved-file scan. Missing or incomplete dependency evidence is a blocker, never an empty-clean audit.
- `promote_niagara_system_candidate(source_system_path, target_system_path, dry_run=true, forbidden_dependency_prefixes=None, forbidden_source_roots=None, allow_non_temp_source=false, allow_temp_target=false, allow_temp_dependencies=false, overwrite_existing=false, save=true, request_compile=true, timeout_seconds=120.0)`
  - Guarded first-pass promotion command for generated Niagara Systems.
  - Dry-run by default. With `dry_run=false`, duplicates the source system to a new target package, registers it, optionally requests compile, saves it, then runs post-promotion dependency audit.
  - Source must be under `/Game/_MCP_Temp/NiagaraGenerated/` by default. Target must be outside `/Game/_MCP_Temp` by default.
  - Overwrite is deliberately unsupported in this first pass.
  - The source temp asset is left untouched; the command duplicates rather than moves.
  - The Python surface strictly binds the response to the requested source, target, dry-run/save/compile flags, temp-policy flags, overwrite policy, forbidden roots, dependency arrays/counts/hits, and exact audit object paths. A transport failure or malformed/contradictory response returns `mutation_state_unknown=true`, `save_state_unknown=true`, `do_not_retry=true`, and exact reload/cleanup/manual-review candidates instead of inferring success. Because a timed-out socket command may still be running in the editor, recovery closes the editor before trusting or reloading on-disk bytes.
  - Durable non-temp promotion requires `save=true` and saved-file dependency evidence after the duplicate is written. It is blocked before mutation otherwise; generated temp targets remain available for isolated multi-step authoring.
- `plan_niagara_promotion_manifest(source_system_path="", source_system_paths=None, target_root="/Game/MCPWeather/Generated", target_system_paths=None, asset_name_prefix="", asset_name_suffix="", forbidden_dependency_prefixes=None, forbidden_source_roots=None, allow_non_temp_source=false, allow_temp_target=false, allow_temp_dependencies=false, write_manifest=false, manifest_name="", timeout_seconds=120.0)`
  - Python orchestration layer for planning one or more Niagara System promotions before writing project content.
  - Runs `promote_niagara_system_candidate(dry_run=true, save=true, request_compile=true)` for each candidate, records target package naming, dependency preflight summaries, and per-entry blockers, and returns `all_can_promote`. These flags describe the default execution policy; dry-run itself performs no save or compile mutation.
  - Does not duplicate, move, save, compile, or delete Unreal assets after every dry-run response is strictly validated. If a dry-run/transport response is unvalidated, read-only/write state is reported unknown, no manifest is written, exact target recovery is required, and automatic retry is forbidden.
  - Optional `write_manifest=true` writes only a JSON report under `MCPGameProject/Saved/MCP/NiagaraPromotionManifests` after all dry-run calls remain in a known state.
  - Target roots must be non-temp `/Game` folders by default; `/Game/_MCP_Temp` requires `allow_temp_target=true`.
- `execute_niagara_promotion_manifest(manifest=None, manifest_path="", confirmation_token="", require_confirmation=true, save=true, request_compile=true, write_execution_report=false, execution_report_name="", timeout_seconds=180.0)`
  - Python orchestration layer for executing a planned Niagara promotion manifest.
  - Requires the exact `confirmation_token` returned by `plan_niagara_promotion_manifest` in all modes; the compatibility field `require_confirmation` must remain `true`, and `false` is rejected before manifest loading or bridge dispatch. The executor then re-runs `promote_niagara_system_candidate(dry_run=true)` for every entry using the exact requested execution `save`/`request_compile` policy before any asset mutation. `save=false` with any non-temp target is rejected before dispatch.
  - If any entry has a known, strictly validated blocker, no promotion is executed. If a revalidation response is malformed or transport state is unknown, the result does not claim that no mutation occurred and instead returns exact reload/inspection recovery.
  - If any entry fails revalidation, no promotion is executed.
  - If all entries pass, calls `promote_niagara_system_candidate(dry_run=false)` entry by entry and returns promoted copy audit results. A partial execution is never automatically retried: it returns `do_not_retry=true`, exact `confirmed_promoted_paths`, and `manual_reconcile_partial_manifest_before_retry`.
  - Supports batch manifests: all entries are revalidated first, then entries execute in manifest order.
  - `manifest_path` must resolve under `MCPGameProject/Saved/MCP/NiagaraPromotionManifests` when loading a saved manifest.
  - Optional `write_execution_report=true` writes only a JSON report under `MCPGameProject/Saved/MCP/NiagaraPromotionManifests/Executions`.
  - Manifest version and policy fields are exact-typed and included in the confirmation token; strings such as `"false"` cannot widen a policy. If the optional execution report cannot be written after promotion, the response preserves confirmed mutation paths and reports failure instead of losing execution evidence.
- `create_empty_niagara_system(target_system_path, allow_non_temp_path=false, overwrite_existing=false, save=true, wait_for_completion=true, timeout_seconds=10.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.1)`
  - Creates a saved empty Niagara System through UE's `UNiagaraSystemFactoryNew` and `AssetTools.CreateAsset`.
  - Refuses existing target assets; overwrite is deliberately unsupported in the first pass.
  - Generated/temp path only by default and returns compile wait details plus a dependency audit.
- `create_empty_niagara_emitter(target_emitter_path, add_default_modules_and_renderers=false, allow_non_temp_path=false, overwrite_existing=false, save=true)`
  - Creates a saved Niagara Emitter through UE's `UNiagaraEmitterFactoryNew`.
  - With `add_default_modules_and_renderers=false`, this is the real empty-emitter path; pass `true` only when the editor default sprite emitter baseline is wanted.
  - Refuses existing target assets and returns a dependency audit.
- `create_basic_sprite_niagara_system(target_system_path, emitter_name="Emitter", material_path="", allow_non_temp_path=false, overwrite_existing=false, save=true, wait_for_completion=true, timeout_seconds=10.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.1)`
  - Creates a saved Niagara System with one default sprite emitter.
  - Uses a non-inheritable transient source emitter copied into the system, so the saved system should not depend on an auxiliary temp emitter asset.
  - Optionally applies a material to the generated sprite renderer and returns parent-reference counts plus a dependency audit.
- `create_sprite_niagara_preset_system(target_system_path, preset="basic", emitter_name="Emitter", material_path="", spawn_rate=None, velocity=None, alignment="", facing_mode="", sub_image_size=None, fixed_bounds_min=None, fixed_bounds_max=None, local_space=None, sprite_size=None, lifetime=None, use_project_weather_materials=false, add_spawn_box_location=None, spawn_box_size=None, spawn_box_offset=None, add_weather_detail_modules=None, allow_non_temp_path=false, overwrite_existing=false, save=true, wait_for_completion=true, timeout_seconds=10.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.1)`
  - Creates a saved Niagara System from a conservative factory sprite preset.
  - Supported presets are `basic`, `rain`, `snow`, `dust`, and `sparks`.
  - Internally creates a factory basic sprite system, edits existing `SpawnRate` and `AddVelocity` RapidIteration inputs, adjusts the sprite renderer, optionally sets fixed bounds/local space, then compiles and saves once.
  - `rain` and `snow` set existing InitializeParticle RapidIteration values by suffix: rain uses `SpriteSize=[5,120]`, `Lifetime=1.8`; snow uses `SpriteSize=[22,22]`, `Lifetime=12`. Override with `sprite_size=[x,y]` and `lifetime=seconds`.
  - When `use_project_weather_materials=true` and `material_path` is empty, rain uses `/Game/MCPWeather/FX/Rain/Materials/M_MCPWeather_Rain_Particle` and snow uses `/Game/MCPWeather/FX/Snow/Materials/M_MCPWeather_Snow_Particle`. This is an explicit project-content dependency, not a plugin dependency, and the response reports `material_source="project_weather_default"`.
  - If `material_path` is provided explicitly, it takes precedence and the response reports `material_source="caller"`. The default is still no material override.
  - `rain` and `snow` insert the stock `/Niagara/Modules/Spawn/Location/BoxLocation.BoxLocation` module by default and set `Box Size` / `Box Offset`; pass `add_spawn_box_location=false` to keep the factory origin-only spawn.
  - `rain` and `snow` also add conservative weather detail modules by default: `Drag`, `GravityForce`, `CurlNoiseForce`, `WindForce`, `ScaleColor`, and `ScaleSpriteSize`. Pass `add_weather_detail_modules=false` to keep only the earlier seed behavior.
  - Refuses existing target assets and is generated/temp path only by default.
  - Current presets are safe starting points, not complete volume/weather solvers: collision, randomized variation, camera-following, material-specific textures, and burst shaping remain later authoring steps.
- `create_niagara_visible_scratch_pad_snow_seed(target_system_path, preset="snow", emitter_name="Emitter", material_path="", use_project_weather_materials=true, scratch_pad_name="MCP_VisibleSizeScratch", parameter_name="Particles.SpriteSize", parameter_value=null, user_parameter_name="User.MCP_VisibleScratchPad_SpriteSize", user_parameter_default_value=null, target_usage="ParticleUpdateScript", save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=true, timeout_seconds=180)`
  - Composite Python recipe for the first visible blank-from-scratch Scratch Pad path.
  - Creates a snow preset seed with BoxLocation and conservative weather detail modules, then runs `create_niagara_scratch_pad_vec2_user_parameter_module` to add a User-driven sprite-size Scratch Pad in `ParticleUpdateScript`.
  - Returns `write_scope="visible_scratch_pad_snow_seed_recipe"` plus both the preset creation result and the nested Scratch Pad recipe result.
  - This is still temp/generated by default and is meant as a repeatable learning fixture, not a final weather-system replacement.
- `cleanup_generated_niagara_assets_offline(package_paths=None, name_prefix="", older_than_minutes=None, dry_run=true, require_editor_closed=true, allow_all=false)`
  - Python-only filesystem cleanup for generated Niagara temp assets under `/Game/_MCP_Temp/NiagaraGenerated`.
  - Dry-run by default and refuses real deletion while `UnrealEditor.exe` or `UnrealEditor-Cmd.exe` is running. If process-state probing fails, the default editor-closed guard fails closed instead of assuming the editor is absent.
  - Deletes only selected `.uasset`, `.uexp`, `.ubulk`, `.uptnl`, `.m.ubulk`, and `.upayload` package segments whose resolved paths stay under the generated Niagara temp root. Explicit paths and prefix scans also discover orphan sidecars when the `.uasset` segment is missing.
  - Real deletion is all-or-nothing at preflight: any invalid/unsafe candidate prevents every unlink. The editor-closed state is checked again immediately before deletion to close the main enumerate-then-delete race window.
- `inspect_niagara_renderers(system_path)`
  - Reads enabled renderer classes, material fields, material slots, and used materials.
- `set_niagara_renderer_material(system_path, material_path, emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", renderer_index=None, material_slot_index=0, allow_source_edit=false, save=true)`
  - Sets a renderer material reference.
  - Refuses source assets by default; pass `allow_source_edit=true` only after review.
- `add_niagara_sprite_renderer(system_path, material_path, emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", alignment="Automatic", facing_mode="FaceCamera", sub_image_size=None, skip_if_existing=true, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true)`
  - Adds one Sprite renderer to a selected emitter.
  - Refuses source assets by default; pass `allow_source_edit=true` only after review.
- `add_niagara_mesh_renderer(system_path, emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", meshes_binding_parameter="User.MeshList", mesh_index_binding="Particles.MeshIndex", mesh_paths=None, skip_if_existing=true, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true)`
  - Adds one Mesh renderer to a selected emitter and can bind `MeshesBinding` to a User Mesh Array such as `User.MeshList`.
  - `mesh_paths` accepts StaticMesh path strings or mesh-entry objects and becomes the renderer fallback mesh list; runtime Blueprint can still override `User.MeshList`.
  - Refuses source assets by default; pass `allow_source_edit=true` only after review.
- `set_niagara_renderer_enabled(system_path, enabled, emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", renderer_index=None, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true)`
  - Enables or disables one renderer without disabling its owning emitter.
- `cleanup_niagara_renderers(system_path, remove_renderer_indices=None, clear_meshes_binding_renderer_indices=None, expected_renderers=None, expected_renderer_count=None, emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", dry_run=true, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=false, timeout_seconds=10.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.1)`
  - Dry-run-first cleanup for exact renderer indices. Every target must match an expected class and enabled state before disabled renderers can be removed or an inert Mesh Renderer `MeshesBinding` can be reset.
  - A clear target's `expected_renderers` entry must also include its current `meshes_binding_parameter`; the command rejects a stale binding value. When compile waiting is requested, a timeout or remaining compile work prevents saving and returns an error.
- `set_niagara_emitter_enabled(system_path, enabled, emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true)`
  - Enables or disables one emitter handle.
- `remove_niagara_emitter(system_path, emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true)`
  - Removes one emitter handle from an authored Niagara System.
- `remove_niagara_modules(system_path, module_names=None, module_name_prefixes=None, module_name_contains=None, module_name="", emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=false, timeout_seconds=10.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.1)`
  - Removes matching stack modules by reconnecting the parameter-map chain and deleting the matched module group. Source assets require `allow_source_edit=true`.
- `remap_niagara_parameter_collection_references(system_path, new_collection_path, old_collection_path="", old_namespace="", allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, replace_object_references=false)`
  - Remaps Niagara graph pins and cached script references from one Niagara Parameter Collection namespace to another.
  - Intended for dependency cleanup after duplicating source systems; refuses source assets by default.
  - `replace_object_references=true` runs a broad UObject reference archive pass and should be reserved for small, reviewed systems.
- `remap_niagara_script_parameter_collection_references(new_collection_path, old_collection_path="", old_namespace="", script_path="", script_paths=None, root_path="", allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=true)`
  - Remaps standalone Niagara Script assets under a root or explicit path list, including graph pins, cached collection references, and cached executable collection path strings.
  - Intended for duplicated module-script cleanup after cloning Marketplace/source Niagara systems into project-owned content.
- `recompile_niagara_scripts_in_root(root_path="", script_paths=None, allow_source_compile=false, force=true, save=true)`
  - Requests compile for Niagara Script assets under a root or explicit path list.
  - Compile requests are limited to generated/temp Niagara content by default; pass `allow_source_compile=true` only after review.
- `repair_niagara_parameter_collection(collection_path, allow_source_edit=false, save=true)`
  - Ensures a Niagara Parameter Collection default instance contains store entries for the collection parameters.
  - Intended after duplicating/remapping NPC assets when default values are missing from the instance store.
- `inspect_niagara_parameter_collection_values(collection_path, parameter_names=None, namespace="", max_parameters=256)`
  - Reads Niagara Parameter Collection default instance values, including missing-store indicators.
- `set_niagara_parameter_collection_values(collection_path, values, namespace="", allow_source_edit=false, save=true)`
  - Sets Niagara Parameter Collection default instance values by parameter name.
  - Refuses source assets by default; pass `allow_source_edit=true` only after review.
- `inspect_niagara_user_parameters(system_path)`
  - Reads exposed `User.*` parameters, types, values, and whether MCP can set them.
- `set_niagara_user_parameter(system_path, parameter_name, value, allow_source_edit=false, save=true)`
  - Sets supported exposed User parameter values.
  - Supports common scalar, vector, color, and object-like values handled by the C++ bridge.
- `upsert_niagara_user_parameters(system_path, parameters, continue_on_error=false, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true)`
  - Creates or updates exposed User parameters, including supported Array Data Interfaces such as `arrayposition` and `arrayfloat3`.
  - Refuses source assets by default.
- `remove_niagara_user_parameters(system_path, parameter_names=null, parameter_name="", dry_run=true, remove_graph_references=true, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=true, timeout_seconds=10.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.1, continue_on_error=false)`
  - Removes exposed `User.*` parameters after a dry-run preview.
  - With `remove_graph_references=true`, Niagara's system-wide removal callback may clear graph, renderer, Data Interface, or simulation-stage bindings that reference the parameter. Use the dry-run result to review the exact exposed variable before apply.
  - Apply requires compile request and completion wait. The command re-reads the exposed store both immediately and after compilation; a recreated parameter returns `success=false` and is not saved.
  - Source-edit protection is checked against both the requested path and the resolved loaded asset path, preventing redirectors from bypassing the default temp-root guard.
- `remove_niagara_unused_module_input_path(system_path, scratch_pad_name, module_name, module_node_guid, input_name, linked_user_parameter_name, custom_hlsl_signature_name, expected_hlsl_identifier_absent, custom_hlsl_input_name="", scratch_pad_script_path="", expected_hlsl_body_hash="", expected_custom_hlsl_node_guid="", expected_override_node_guid="", expected_input_type="", expected_user_source_node_guid="", expected_scratch_map_get_node_guids=null, dry_run=true, allow_source_edit=false, save=false, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=true, timeout_seconds=10.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.1)`
  - Removes one exact, proven-unused chain: exposed `User.*` parameter -> emitter-stack module override -> Scratch Pad `Module.*` metadata/ParameterMapGet -> Custom HLSL signature input.
  - The first call must use `dry_run=true`. Copy `expected_hlsl_body_hash`, `expected_custom_hlsl_node_guid`, `expected_override_node_guid`, `expected_input_type`, `expected_user_source_node_guid`, and `expected_scratch_map_get_node_guids` from `discovery_contract` into the apply call. Apply fails closed if any selector, type, GUID, link, metadata entry, HLSL body hash, or guarded HLSL identifier has changed.
  - This narrow command supports value inputs only. Object/Data Interface inputs, shared Scratch Pads, direct User ParameterMapGet nodes with other semantic outputs, and mismatched HLSL guard names are rejected. `expected_hlsl_identifier_absent` must exactly equal the selected Custom HLSL input name.
  - It removes only the selected direct User ParameterMapGet node, its exact graph metadata entry when present, and the exposed store entry. It does not call Niagara's system-wide variable-removal callback, so renderer, Data Interface, and simulation-stage bindings are not silently rewritten.
  - The HLSL body itself is never edited. Apply requires compile request plus completion wait, then re-reads the exposed store, User/source metadata, emitter override, Scratch Pad metadata/pins/signature, and exact HLSL string before optional save. Saving defaults to false and is allowed only after compile/readback gates pass.
  - Source-edit protection is checked against both the requested path and the resolved loaded asset path.
  - A post-mutation failure is never saved. The response reports `mutation_applied_in_memory=true` and `requires_reload_or_undo=true`; reload the package or undo before retrying.
  - This first implementation accepts only a system-owned Scratch Pad and a direct `User.*` ParameterMapGet override source. It is intentionally not a general Niagara graph deletion API.
- `inspect_niagara_stack(system_path, include_pins=false, max_function_calls=200)`
  - Reads system, emitter, and Scratch Pad function-call stack metadata.
- `inspect_niagara_graph(system_path, include_pins=true, include_links=true, include_scratch_pads=true, max_nodes_per_graph=600, max_links_per_graph=2000)`
  - Reads full Niagara graph node, pin, and link topology for system scripts, emitter graphs, and Scratch Pad scripts.
  - This is read-only and intended as the structured basis for future safe graph authoring.
- `inspect_niagara_graph_actions(system_path, scratch_pad_name="", scratch_pad_script_path="", scratch_pad_script_index=null, safe_only=true, search_text="", max_actions=600, include_canonical=false, include_template_pins=false)`
  - Exposes UE 5.6's native Niagara graph-menu action inventory for one system-owned Scratch Pad without modifying the graph.
  - Each action has a stable content-derived `action_id`, native node class, operator/function identity, categories, and a `recipe_safe` flag. `safe_only=true` is the recommended default.
  - `safe_only=false` is discovery-only: seeing an engine action does not authorize it for graph mutation.
  - `include_template_pins=true` transiently materializes the first 200 returned action templates and exposes their native input/output pins without touching the asset graph.
- `apply_niagara_scratch_pad_graph_recipe(system_path, custom_hlsl_node_guid, nodes, links, output_mappings, scratch_pad_name="", scratch_pad_script_path="", scratch_pad_script_index=null, expected_hlsl_body_hash="", dry_run=true, remove_custom_hlsl=true, save=true, request_compile=true, timeout_seconds=30.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.05)`
  - Applies native Niagara operation, conversion, select, reroute, or non-MCP function-call nodes to exactly one Custom HLSL node in `/Game/_MCP_Temp/NiagaraGenerated` only.
  - Start with `dry_run=true`, then pass its exact `expected_hlsl_body_hash` to apply. The selected Scratch Pad must have a direct enabled function-call reference reachable by walking input links backward from a real system/emitter output. A path containing `NiagaraNodeStaticSwitch`, `NiagaraNodeUsageSelector`, `NiagaraNodeSimTargetSelector`, or `NiagaraNodeSelect` is treated as unresolved and rejected before mutation; unreferenced or indirect-only scripts are also rejected because standalone Scratch Pad compilation does not reliably reproduce their UE 5.6 stack context.
  - Every owning-system compile uses non-force `RequestCompile(false)`. Before each required compile, every caller script's pending `ComputedId` must differ from the clean baseline. After compilation, that caller's `CachedId` and `ComputedId` must both equal the captured pending `ComputedId`, remain `UpToDate`, and preserve the baseline error/warning/unknown-count contract. This proves that the compiled data consumed the intended graph mutation without rotating IDs through a force rebuild.
  - Dependency auditing runs both before mutation and again on the final native graph before save. The final audit uses a non-mutating save-contract archive with an explicit read-only weak-reference pass and includes graph function calls, serialized node hard/soft/weak object and type references, pin type/default object/string/text references, selected-function transitive packages, and direct system dependencies; incomplete traversal or any MCP-only dependency fails closed.
  - A post-mutation failure attempts structural restoration of the original Custom HLSL node, node membership/order, graph fingerprint, references, and schema links, then performs a non-force recovery compile. This is not reported as a clean/full rollback: serialized Niagara IDs and traversal caches cannot be proven identical to disk, so the exact temp package remains dirty with `rollback_verified=false`, `requires_package_reload=true`, `undo_recovery_unproven=true`, `do_not_retry=true`, and a reload-required rollback policy. Do not save, retry, or rely on Undo alone; reload the exact package from disk first.
  - The per-phase timeout is normalized to the same finite 1-60 second range used by the bridge, and the Python wrapper budgets for baseline, pre-removal, final, and recovery waits plus a 30-second transport margin. If the socket/transport result becomes indeterminate after dispatch, the command may still be running: it returns `mutation_state_unknown=true`, `save_state_unknown=true`, `command_may_still_be_in_flight=true`, and `do_not_retry=true`. Close the editor and confirm process exit before trusting, hashing, reloading, or exactly cleaning the target package.
  - Node `x`/`y` values must be finite and within +/-1,000,000 before any float/int graph-position conversion. Compile status snapshots do not repeat the explicit phase wait, so the external timeout budget still covers the real worst-case wait sequence.
  - If `SaveLoadedAsset` fails, the response treats persisted state as unknown even after in-memory rollback: `save_state_unknown=true`, exact package reload, editor-close, exact offline sidecar cleanup, and disposable ghost recreation are required. Automatic save/retry is forbidden.
  - Live safety checks treat independent graph, dirty-package, and disk-hash evidence as authoritative over the response envelope. A changed in-memory package requires every observed exact package to be reloaded. If saved package bytes diverge, reload is explicitly not described as restoration; the report switches to `manual_restore_or_known_good_copy_required` and lists the changed source/ghost package segments.
  - Endpoint kinds are `node` and `custom_hlsl_input`; direct pass-through HLSL can therefore be replaced without adding a redundant native node. The output mapping must preserve every consumed output being converted.
  - The authored asset contains native Niagara nodes only and has no UnrealMCP runtime dependency. This is a guarded ghost-test primitive, not a source-asset rewrite API.
- `inspect_niagara_scratch_pad_interface(system_path, include_graph_summary=true, include_parent_scratch_pads=true, max_scripts=200, max_function_calls=80)`
  - Reads Scratch Pad ownership, usage, supported usage contexts, inputs, outputs, control hints, and optional compact graph summaries.
  - This is read-only and intended as the authoring-interface basis for future Scratch Pad duplication and graph wiring.
- `duplicate_or_attach_emitter_from_source(target_system_path, source_emitter_path="", source_system_path="", source_emitter_index=None, source_emitter_name="", new_emitter_name="", enabled=None, copy_source_user_parameters=false, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true)`
  - Adds a source Niagara Emitter asset or a source Niagara System emitter handle into a target generated temp Niagara System.
  - Refuses target systems outside `/Game/_MCP_Temp/NiagaraGenerated/` by default.
  - Source assets are read-only; only the target system is modified, compiled, and optionally saved.
  - Uses Niagara Editor's native add-emitter route so the system spawn/update graphs are rebuilt with the new emitter nodes. Direct handle insertion is intentionally avoided because it can leave a compiled emitter permanently disabled at runtime even though the handle itself reports enabled.
  - When copying from `source_system_path`, `copy_source_user_parameters=true` copies source `User.*` defaults into the target system. Data Interface user parameters are copied into target-owned Data Interface objects instead of preserving source-private object references.
  - Private Scratch Pad scripts referenced by duplicated source emitters are localized into the target temp system and graph function-call references are rewritten before save, preventing illegal private-object references back into the source system.
- `inspect_niagara_event_handlers(system_path, emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", max_handlers=256)`
  - Read-only Event Handler topology inspection, including target/source emitter IDs, source event, execution/spawn limits, event-script usage ID, graph path, and output-node existence.
  - Also reports source spawn/update event-generator names, exact generator matching, event-script CPU readiness, and system emitter execution/overlap order. Use the reported generator name as the handler source name; for example, UE 5.6 Collision may compile as `CollisionEvent` rather than the shorter display label `Collision`.
  - Works on existing source systems without enabling mutation.
- `set_niagara_emitter_persistent_ids(system_path, enabled, emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=true, timeout_seconds=60, poll_interval_seconds=0.1)`
  - Enables stable `Particles.ID` generation for a CPU emitter. Niagara Collision Event generation requires this on the source emitter.
  - The setting is reported by `inspect_niagara_emitter_properties` as `requires_persistent_ids`; mutation remains generated-temp-only by default.
  - The requested path and resolved loaded path are both checked against the temp root. Durable save requires compile request plus completion wait and a separate read-only compile-status snapshot; compile failure, timeout, incomplete readback, or save failure returns a reload-required recovery contract instead of persisting a broken result.
- `add_niagara_event_handler(system_path, emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", source_emitter_index=None, source_emitter_name="", source_emitter_id="", source_event_name="CollisionEvent", execution_mode="SpawnedParticles", spawn_number=1, max_events_per_frame=64, random_spawn_number=false, min_spawn_number=0, update_attribute_initial_values=true, skip_if_duplicate=true, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=true, timeout_seconds=60, poll_interval_seconds=0.1)`
  - Creates an engine-native CPU Event Handler through UE 5.6's standard emitter event-script API; generated content does not retain an UnrealMCP dependency.
  - Mutation is restricted to `/Game/_MCP_Temp/NiagaraGenerated/` unless `allow_source_edit=true`. GPU source/target emitters, ambiguous selectors, invalid spawn ranges, and conflicting duplicate consumers are rejected.
  - The requested and resolved target paths are both guarded. `save=true` requires compile request, completion wait, and a separate read-only compile-status snapshot; save occurs only after compile, output-node, CPU-script, and exact source-generator readback pass. Failure remains unsaved and requires exact-package reload before retry.
  - Pass the returned `target_usage_id` to `add_niagara_stock_module_to_stack(..., target_usage="ParticleEventScript", target_usage_id=<id>)` to populate the handler with an engine or project module such as `ReceiveCollisionEvent`.
  - `smoke_niagara_event_handler_live.py live` is the repeatable temp-only contract proof. It authors Rain → analytical-plane `CollisionEvent` → event-only receiver, requires clean compile/topology/promotion audit, and proves positive receiver runtime spawn counters with receiver `SpawnRate` absent. It deletes only its exact transient preview actor while the editor is open; package cleanup uses the script's `cleanup` mode after editor shutdown.
- `create_niagara_system_from_source_template(target_system_path, source_system_path, source_emitter_indices=None, copy_source_user_parameters=true, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=true, timeout_seconds=180)`
  - One-call source-template path: duplicates the full `source_system_path` Niagara System into a new generated temp package, preserving system scripts, system RapidIteration values, user defaults, emitters, renderers, Scratch Pads, and system properties.
  - When `source_emitter_indices` is provided, the wrapper duplicates the whole source system first and then removes unselected emitters from the generated temp copy. This keeps system-level stack context intact for project-authored weather/FX systems.
  - The `copy_source_user_parameters` flag is retained for API compatibility; source `User.*` defaults are inherently preserved by the full-system duplicate route.
  - This is the preferred path for project-authored weather/FX template seeds such as `/Game/MCPWeather` where stock modules alone do not reproduce the source system.
  - Once duplicate/promotion mutation is dispatched, an exception, missing response, or incomplete follow-up returns `niagara_system_template_creation_state_unknown` with `do_not_retry=true`, exact-target reload guidance, and exact-path offline cleanup requirements. A caller must stop the run; a late editor completion must not escape cleanup ownership.
  - Promotion success is accepted only when response mode, save/compile request flags, mutation fields, source/target/promoted package bindings, and the post-promotion dependency audit agree exactly. Save failure and post-promotion dependency failure return structured reload/cleanup recovery. Unexpected generated-temp paths remain explicit cleanup candidates; non-generated or malformed returned paths are preserved separately for manual review and never enter automatic temp cleanup.
- `create_niagara_scratch_pad_vec2_user_parameter_module(target_system_path, scratch_pad_name="MCP_BlankUpdateScratch", parameter_name="Particles.SpriteSize", parameter_value=null, user_parameter_name="User.MCP_BlankScratchPad_SpriteSize", user_parameter_default_value=null, target_usage="ParticleUpdateScript", target_stack_emitter_index=0, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=true, timeout_seconds=180)`
  - Composite Python recipe for the first reusable blank Scratch Pad User-parameter authoring path.
  - Creates a blank target-local Scratch Pad module, adds one Vector2D `ParameterMapSet` write, creates/defaults a matching `User.*` parameter, links it through `ParameterMapGet`, inserts the module into the requested stack, saves, and optionally waits for compile.
  - Returns `write_scope="scratch_pad_vec2_user_parameter_module_recipe"` plus per-stage results so tests can still inspect each primitive.
  - This is intentionally Vector2D-only for now; use the lower-level primitives when testing other parameter types or custom graph shapes.
- `create_niagara_scratch_pad_color_user_parameter_module(target_system_path, scratch_pad_name="MCP_ColorScratch", parameter_name="Particles.Color", parameter_value=null, user_parameter_name="User.MCP_ScratchPad_Color", user_parameter_default_value=null, target_usage="ParticleUpdateScript", target_stack_emitter_index=0, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=true, timeout_seconds=180)`
  - Scratch Pad color User-link public temp route for the reviewed `Particles.Color` Linear Color shape.
  - Creates a blank target-local Scratch Pad module, adds one Linear Color `ParameterMapSet` write, creates/defaults a matching `User.*` parameter, links it through `ParameterMapGet`, inserts the module into the requested stack, saves, and optionally waits for compile.
  - Returns `write_scope="scratch_pad_color_user_parameter_module_recipe"` plus per-stage results.
  - This is generated/temp-system only by default, keeps overwrite/source edits disabled, and does not admit arbitrary Scratch Pad graph synthesis.
- `create_niagara_scratch_pad_bool_user_parameter_module(target_system_path, scratch_pad_name="MCP_BoolUserScratch", parameter_name="Particles.MCPBoolProbe", parameter_value=null, module_input_name="MCPBoolInput", module_input_default_value=null, user_parameter_name="User.MCP_ScratchPad_Bool", user_parameter_default_value=null, target_usage="ParticleUpdateScript", target_stack_emitter_index=0, overwrite_existing=false, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=true, timeout_seconds=180)`
  - Scratch Pad bool User-link public temp route for runtime toggles and branch-style controls.
  - Creates a blank target-local Scratch Pad module, writes a bool `ParameterMapSet` pin such as `Particles.MCPBoolProbe`, creates a reachable `Module.*` bool input through `add_niagara_scratch_pad_module_input`, inserts the module into the stack, then binds that stack-exposed input to a `User.*` bool through `set_niagara_module_input_user_parameter`.
  - Returns `write_scope="scratch_pad_bool_user_parameter_module_recipe"` plus per-stage results and the inserted module node GUID.
  - This is generated/temp-system only by default and does not admit arbitrary Scratch Pad graph synthesis or overwrite existing module-input override graphs unless `overwrite_existing=true` is explicit.
- `create_niagara_scratch_pad_bool_visible_toggle_module(target_system_path, scratch_pad_name="MCP_BoolVisibleScratch", parameter_name="Particles.SpriteSize", parameter_value=null, base_module_input_name="MCPBaseSpriteSize", base_module_input_default_value=null, user_parameter_name="User.MCP_VisibleToggle", user_parameter_default_value=null, custom_hlsl_input_name="MCPVisibleToggle", custom_hlsl_expression="BaseValue * (MCPVisibleToggle ? 1.0 : 0.0)", custom_hlsl_output_pin_name="MCPVisibleSize", custom_hlsl_signature_name="MCP_ScratchPadBoolVisibleSize", target_usage="ParticleUpdateScript", target_stack_emitter_index=0, overwrite_existing=false, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=true, timeout_seconds=180)`
  - Scratch Pad bool visible-toggle public temp route for the reviewed `Particles.SpriteSize` shape.
  - Creates a blank target-local Scratch Pad module, writes `Particles.SpriteSize`, links that pin to a reachable vec2 `Module.MCPBaseSpriteSize` BaseValue, upserts `User.MCP_VisibleToggle`, then wraps `Particles.SpriteSize` with a Custom HLSL dynamic input using `BaseValue * (MCPVisibleToggle ? 1.0 : 0.0)`.
  - Returns `write_scope="scratch_pad_bool_visible_toggle_module_recipe"` plus Custom HLSL node/readback metadata and the inserted module node GUID.
  - This is generated/temp-system only by default. It admits exactly the reviewed bool visible-toggle Custom HLSL shape; arbitrary Scratch Pad graph synthesis remains closed. The optional live preview comparison captures transient `User.MCP_VisibleToggle=true/false` frames without persisting preview-only overrides, and the guarded release-candidate smoke can promote the reviewed shape to an explicit non-temp target through the confirmation-token manifest path.
- `create_or_duplicate_scratch_pad_module(target_system_path, source_script_path="", source_system_path="", source_owner_kind="system", source_script_index=None, source_scratch_pad_name="", source_emitter_index=None, source_emitter_name="", target_owner_kind="system", target_emitter_index=None, target_emitter_name="", new_script_name="", target_supported_usage="ParticleUpdateScript", allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true)`
  - Creates a blank target-local Scratch Pad module from the engine default module template when no source is provided, or duplicates an existing Scratch Pad script when `source_script_path` or `source_system_path` is provided.
  - Refuses target systems outside `/Game/_MCP_Temp/NiagaraGenerated/` by default.
  - Blank creation sets the module's supported usage context from `target_supported_usage`, so it can be inserted into a matching stack afterward.
  - This pass only creates/duplicates the Scratch Pad script. Use `add_scratch_pad_module_to_stack` to insert a target-local module into a stack after creation or duplication.
- `create_niagara_ndc_reader_scratch_pad_module(system_path, scratch_pad_name, data_channel_asset_path, stage="particle_spawn_read", position_variable="Position", velocity_variable="Velocity", spawn_count_variable="SpawnCount", event_type_variable="EventType", position_target="Particles.Position", velocity_target="Particles.Velocity", spawn_count_target="Particles.NDCSpawnCount", event_type_target="Particles.NDCEventType", read_success_target="Particles.NDCReadSuccess", read_current_frame=false, dry_run=false, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true)`
  - Creates one new system-owned Scratch Pad from UE's pristine four-node `DefaultModuleScript` and mirrors one stage of the UE 5.6 Niagara Data Channel Wizard. `emitter_spawn_init` stores `Module.DataChannel` in `Emitter.SpawnDataChannel`; `emitter_update_spawn` calls `SpawnDirect` with `VarName=<spawn_count_variable>` and `VarType=int`; `particle_spawn_read` wires `GetNDCSpawnData -> Read` and maps all four requested fields plus read success. For V02's two emitters, select `DebrisCount` or `DustCount` per update/read module; a generic `SpawnCount` field is not required.
  - The three stages must be created and inserted in canonical order: `emitter_spawn_init` in `EmitterSpawnScript`, `emitter_update_spawn` in `EmitterUpdateScript`, then `particle_spawn_read` in `ParticleSpawnScript` for the same emitter. The command returns each exact `target_usage` and Scratch Pad path.
  - It validates the target system, the engine template, the required DI signatures, a Global NDC, and exact field types (`Position`, `Vector`, `int`, `int`) before mutation. With `read_current_frame=false`, the channel must keep previous-frame data. Extra NDC fields are allowed.
  - Generated/temp systems are mandatory by default. Scratch Pad names must be ASCII identifiers and must not already exist anywhere in the target system; overwrite and update-in-place are deliberately unsupported. `dry_run=true` performs all preflight checks without creating a UObject, dirtying a package, requesting compile, or saving.
  - Internal authoring happens on a transient duplicate; only the fully wired module is copied into the system. The response includes full channel schema, mappings, graph/node/link counts, created function nodes, Scratch Pad interface readback, and `required_follow_up`.
  - Stack insertion and the first DI object binding remain explicit guarded operations. After all three creation calls, call `add_scratch_pad_module_to_stack` with the returned path/usage. Then call `set_niagara_data_interface_module_input` only on the inserted `emitter_spawn_init` module, using input `DataChannel` and properties `{"Channel":"/Game/.../NDC_Name.NDC_Name","bReadCurrentFrame":false}`. The other stages default-bind to `Emitter.SpawnDataChannel` exactly as the engine wizard does.
  - The particle module deliberately does not add a world-to-simulation Position transform. Keep the lab emitter in world space (`local_space=false`); a guarded transform-node extension is required before using this module in local-space emitters.
- `add_scratch_pad_module_to_stack(target_system_path, scratch_pad_script_path="", scratch_pad_owner_kind="system", scratch_pad_script_index=None, scratch_pad_name="", scratch_pad_emitter_index=None, scratch_pad_emitter_name="", target_usage="ParticleUpdateScript", target_usage_id="", target_emitter_index=None, target_emitter_name="", target_index=None, suggested_name="", allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, skip_if_duplicate=true)`
  - Inserts an existing target-local Scratch Pad module into a Niagara stack through `FNiagaraStackGraphUtilities::AddScriptModuleToStack`.
  - Refuses target systems outside `/Game/_MCP_Temp/NiagaraGenerated/` by default.
  - Requires `UNiagaraScript` usage `Module` and validates that the Scratch Pad advertises support for the requested target usage before adding the function-call node.
  - Skips duplicate insertion by default when the same Scratch Pad script already exists in the requested output stack, including `target_usage_id` when provided, returning `skipped_duplicate=true` and the existing module node metadata without saving or requesting compile.
  - Does not perform arbitrary internal Scratch Pad graph mutation or pin/link rewiring beyond the stack utility insertion.
- `add_niagara_scratch_pad_assignment_module_to_stack(target_system_path, parameter_name="Particles.SpriteSize", parameter_type="vec2", default_value="50.000000,50.000000", target_usage="ParticleUpdateScript", target_usage_id="", target_emitter_index=None, target_emitter_name="", target_index=None, skip_if_duplicate=true, allow_assignment_module_route="", allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=true)`
  - Token-gated assignment-module route through `FNiagaraStackGraphUtilities::AddParameterModuleToStack`.
  - Refuses by default unless `allow_assignment_module_route="ALLOW_SCRATCH_PAD_ASSIGNMENT_MODULE_ROUTE"` is provided, and still refuses non-temp targets unless `allow_source_edit=true`.
  - Currently admits only four guarded single-target shapes: `Particles.SpriteSize` as `vec2` with default `50.000000,50.000000`, `Particles.Color` as `Linear Color` with default `1.000000,1.000000,1.000000,1.000000`, `Particles.Lifetime` as `float` with default `5.000000`, or `Particles.Velocity` as `vec3` with default `0.000000,0.000000,100.000000`.
  - Skips duplicates by default when a matching assignment target already exists in the requested output stack.
  - The tool surface, admission preflight, temp live proof, and cleanup proof are tracked by the assignment-module route contract; broad Scratch Pad graph synthesis remains closed.
- `add_niagara_scratch_pad_parameter_write(system_path, parameter_name, value=null, parameter_type="vec2", default_value="", scratch_pad_script_path="", scratch_pad_owner_kind="system", scratch_pad_script_index=None, scratch_pad_name="", scratch_pad_emitter_index=None, scratch_pad_emitter_name="", skip_if_exists=true, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true)`
  - Adds a `NiagaraNodeParameterMapSet` inside a target-local Scratch Pad module and wires the module `InputMap` through it to the module `OutputMap`.
  - Creates one namespaced parameter input such as `Particles.SpriteSize`, sets its default value, and requests compile/save when enabled.
  - Refuses target systems outside `/Game/_MCP_Temp/NiagaraGenerated/` by default.
  - Skips without mutation when the same Scratch Pad already writes `parameter_name` and `skip_if_exists=true`.
  - This is a narrow first graph-authoring primitive for fresh blank Scratch Pads, not a general-purpose graph editor.
- `add_niagara_scratch_pad_module_input(system_path, input_name, default_value, input_type="bool", consumer_pin_name="", scratch_pad_script_path="", scratch_pad_owner_kind="system", scratch_pad_script_index=None, scratch_pad_name="", scratch_pad_emitter_index=None, scratch_pad_emitter_name="", require_consumer_link=true, overwrite_existing_link=false, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=false, timeout_seconds=10.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.1)`
  - Adds a `Module.*` input read inside a target-local Scratch Pad module by creating a `ParameterMapGet` output with a typed default value.
  - Links the new module input output to an existing consumer pin, usually a matching `ParameterMapSet` value pin such as `Particles.MCPBoolProbe` or a `CustomHLSL` input pin such as `WaveSpeed`, so stack traversal exposes the input for normal module-input inspection and override.
  - Refuses source assets by default and rejects unqualified non-`Module.*` inputs. Unqualified names are normalized to `Module.<name>`.
  - Does not open arbitrary Scratch Pad graph synthesis; it is a narrow module-input producer used before `set_niagara_module_input_literal_override`.
- `add_niagara_scratch_pad_di_variadic_input(system_path, scratch_pad_name, function_node_guid, expected_function_name, expected_di_class, expected_existing_inputs, pin_name, module_input_name, expected_referencing_module_node_guid, default_value=0, input_type="int", scratch_pad_script_path="", expected_input_map_node_guid="", expected_output_node_guid="", allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=true, timeout_seconds=60.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.1)`
  - Atomically adds exactly one `int` variadic input to an existing signature-only Data Interface function call, then creates a `Module.*` `ParameterMapGet` read and links it to that new pin.
  - Requires exact pre-mutation fingerprints: the function node GUID/name/DI class, every existing signature input's name/type/source-node GUID/source-pin name, and the single stack module node GUID that references the target system-owned Scratch Pad.
  - Rejects existing signature pins, graph pins, Scratch Pad metadata, or `ParameterMapGet` outputs with the requested names. It also verifies that all original data links and both ParameterMap exec links survive the signature refresh.
  - Requires exactly one module `InputMap` node and one module `Output` node. Optional expected GUIDs can pin both nodes to an earlier inspection result.
  - Signature preflight reports reflected field-level current/reconstructed export-text diffs. Functional fields remain strict. Besides editor descriptions/source identity and transient `bHidden`, `Inputs` may ignore only an empty-versus-all-zero default payload on a variadic pin whose name/order/type and exact expected single-link fingerprint are proven; base required inputs and nonzero payloads remain exact. `Outputs` raw reflection differences are ignored only when export text plus count/order/name/type are identical.
  - Always requires a clean package and idle Niagara compiler. The non-empty pre-mutation script baseline must also be warning/error-free, `UpToDate`, and have valid matching cached/computed IDs for every known script; dirty, busy, or unsynchronized overrides are intentionally unsupported.
  - `save=true` requires compile request + wait. Saving occurs only after graph readback, DI CDO base-signature/UE `RefreshSignature` equivalence, a changed computed compile ID, and final idle, warning-free, synchronized snapshots. A false `RequestCompile` launch result is diagnostic only, so a DDC/cache-hit or already-completed compile can pass on final evidence.
  - Any post-mutation failure removes the created node/metadata/pins and restores the original signature, but reports rollback success only after the restored graph recompiles to idle/synchronized data, the clean package reloads, and the reloaded baseline structure/signature and compile state are verified. Any incomplete rollback remains visibly dirty and reports mutation state as unknown/present.
  - Example `expected_existing_inputs` entry: `{"pin_name":"Emit","type":"bool","linked_node_guid":"12D639DB-480F-FB27-011E-72BD9A3B0AE3","linked_pin_name":"Particles.NDCDoBurst"}`. For a Data Channel `Append`, include the DI interface input and every existing variadic field in signature order.
- `add_niagara_stock_module_to_stack(target_system_path, module_script_path, target_usage="ParticleSpawnScriptInterpolated", target_usage_id="", target_emitter_index=None, target_emitter_name="", target_index=None, suggested_name="", allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, skip_if_duplicate=true)`
  - Inserts an existing Niagara Module script asset into a system/emitter stack through `FNiagaraStackGraphUtilities::AddScriptModuleToStack`.
  - Use this for stock engine/project modules such as `/Niagara/Modules/Spawn/Location/BoxLocation.BoxLocation` before setting their module inputs.
  - Refuses target systems outside `/Game/_MCP_Temp/NiagaraGenerated/` by default.
  - Requires `UNiagaraScript` usage `Module` and validates that the module advertises support for the requested target usage before adding the function-call node.
  - Skips duplicate insertion by default when the same module script already exists in the requested output stack.
- `set_niagara_scratch_pad_function_input_default(system_path, function_name="", input_pin_name="", value=null, default_value="", function_node_guid="", function_node_index=None, function_call_index=None, scratch_pad_script_path="", scratch_pad_owner_kind="system", scratch_pad_script_index=None, scratch_pad_name="", scratch_pad_emitter_index=None, scratch_pad_emitter_name="", break_links=true, allow_multi_link_break=false, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true)`
  - Sets one internal function-call input pin default inside a target-local Scratch Pad graph.
  - Optionally breaks existing links from that input pin; this is intended for narrow diagnostic probes such as replacing `RenderGrid.SetRenderTargetValue.Value` with a constant color.
  - Requires an explicit Scratch Pad selector: `scratch_pad_script_path`, `scratch_pad_name`, or `scratch_pad_script_index`.
  - Refuses source assets by default; use generated temp systems where possible and pass `allow_source_edit=true` only after review.
- `link_niagara_scratch_pad_pin_to_user_parameter(system_path, target_pin_name, user_parameter_name, scratch_pad_script_path="", scratch_pad_owner_kind="system", scratch_pad_script_index=None, scratch_pad_name="", scratch_pad_emitter_index=None, scratch_pad_emitter_name="", target_node_guid="", target_node_index=None, parameter_map_set_index=None, default_value=None, overwrite_existing=false, allow_multi_link_break=false, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true)`
  - Links one Scratch Pad `ParameterMapSet` input pin to a matching `User.*` parameter by adding a `ParameterMapGet` node.
  - Intended for narrow Grid2D controls such as feeding `AdvectGrid.Local.Module.AdvectionAmount` from a runtime field-scroll parameter.
  - Requires an explicit Scratch Pad selector and refuses to replace existing pin links unless `overwrite_existing=true` is passed.
  - Refuses source assets by default; use generated temp systems where possible and pass `allow_source_edit=true` only after review.
- `replace_niagara_custom_hlsl(system_path, replacement_hlsl, node_guid="", signature_name="", contains_text="", scratch_pad_name="", source_path_contains="", expected_contains="", dry_run=true, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, timeout_seconds=30.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.05, max_hlsl_chars=8000)`
  - Replaces exactly one selected Custom HLSL node. Dry-run remains the default, and an already-equal replacement returns an explicit verified no-op without compiling or saving.
  - A real write verifies exact HLSL readback, node ChangeId rotation, and at least one dependent script Compile ID invalidation before reporting mutation success.
  - With `request_compile=true`, the command waits for completion and requires every affected script's cached executable Compile ID to change and match the post-edit computed Compile ID. A valid DDC result is accepted; elapsed time alone is not treated as proof or failure.
  - UE 5.6.1 source-only Emitter Spawn/Update scripts are reported in `source_only_compile_inputs`, not counted as standalone executable scripts. Their corresponding System Spawn/Update owner must be invalidated and pass the same executable-ID checks; missing owner coverage fails closed (`source_only_owners_covered=false`).
  - Saving happens only after write and compile postconditions pass. The result exposes `mutation_performed`, `readback_verified`, `source_invalidation_verified`, `compile_launched`, `compile_completed`, `compile_effect_verified`, `saved`, and final `verification_pass`; `success=true` requires the applicable postconditions.
  - A failed postcondition returns the complete evidence payload with `success=false` and leaves an unsaved in-memory mutation dirty when the write already occurred, allowing review or editor undo instead of silently persisting an unverified result.
- `inspect_niagara_compile_status(system_path, request_compile=false, force=false, allow_source_compile=false, wait_for_completion=false, timeout_seconds=10.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.1)`
  - Reads per-script Niagara compile statuses, warning/error counts, and outstanding compile request state.
  - `request_compile=true` is blocked for source assets unless `allow_source_compile=true` is explicitly passed.
  - `wait_for_completion=true` polls outstanding compile requests up to `timeout_seconds` and reports `wait_timed_out`.
- `inspect_niagara_simulation_stages(system_path, include_compile_data=true, include_script_compile_status=true, max_stages=128)`
  - Reads emitter SimulationStage objects, generic stage settings, Data Interface bindings, iteration settings, dispatch settings, optional script compile status, and optional `FillCompilationData()` output.
  - This is read-only and is intended for RenderTarget/Data Interface workflows where Niagara editor UI fields are protected or awkward to inspect manually.
- `add_niagara_grid_simulation_stage(system_path, emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", stage_name="MCP_GridSimulationStage", data_interface_name="Emitter.Grid2D Collection", insert_index=None, skip_if_duplicate=true, enabled=true, iteration_source="DataInterface", execute_behavior="Always", num_iterations=1, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=false)`
  - Creates one generic Grid2D DataInterface SimulationStage, binds its iteration source to a Grid2D Collection variable, resets the stage output graph, and returns the `ParticleSimulationStageScript` usage id for follow-up Scratch Pad stack insertion.
  - Refuses source assets by default. Use generated/temp systems first, then pass `allow_source_edit=true` only for reviewed promotion edits.
- `remove_niagara_simulation_stage(system_path, emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", stage_index=None, stage_name="", allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=false)`
  - Removes one SimulationStage and its associated stage graph nodes. This is intended for temp iteration cleanup and guarded to generated/temp assets by default.
- `remove_niagara_scratch_pad_script(system_path, scratch_pad_name="", scratch_pad_owner_kind="any", scratch_pad_script_index=None, scratch_pad_emitter_index=None, scratch_pad_emitter_name="", force=false, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=false)`
  - Removes one target-local Scratch Pad script by name/index, mainly for cleaning orphan scratch pads left by temp graph-authoring probes. Refuses source assets unless `allow_source_edit=true` and refuses referenced scripts unless `force=true`.
- `set_niagara_simulation_stage_settings(system_path, emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", stage_index=None, stage_name="", enabled=None, iteration_source="", data_interface_name="", direct_dispatch_type="", direct_dispatch_element_type="", execute_behavior="", element_count=None, element_count_x=None, element_count_y=None, element_count_z=None, num_iterations=None, num_iterations_binding="", gpu_dispatch_force_linear=None, override_gpu_dispatch_num_threads=None, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true)`
  - Edits one generic SimulationStage setting set, intended for generated/temp diagnostic systems.
  - Refuses source assets by default and requires an explicit stage selector through `stage_index` or `stage_name`.
  - Supports narrow stage controls needed for RT/Data Interface diagnosis: enabled state, iteration source, Grid2D DataInterface binding, direct dispatch type, direct dispatch element type, execute behavior, element counts, iteration count, optional existing `User.*` int iteration binding, and GPU dispatch flags.
  - `num_iterations` alone restores a constant iteration count and clears a prior binding. Passing both `num_iterations=1` and `num_iterations_binding="User.MyInt"` stores `1` as the safe fallback and binds the stage to that existing System User int parameter.
  - Returns before/after stage settings plus `FillCompilationData()` snapshots so direct-dispatch changes can be verified without opening the Niagara editor UI.
- `inspect_niagara_module_inputs(system_path, include_linked_sources=true, include_resolved_stack_inputs=false, max_modules=200, max_candidates_per_module=24, max_resolved_inputs_per_module=8, max_top_candidates=80)`
  - Reads module input candidates for generation planning.
  - Candidate rows are read-only inspection records. `can_author_now=false` means the inspection command itself does not mutate assets; check `dedicated_authoring_tools_available`, `dedicated_authoring_tools`, `authoring_route_hint`, and `authoring_status` to select the supported mutation tool for scalar/vector/color/bool RapidIteration inputs, User-parameter links, or RenderTarget2D Data Interface inputs.
- `inspect_niagara_data_interface_overrides(system_path, input_name="", emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", module_index=None, module_name="", module_node_guid="", max_modules=200, max_inputs_per_module=64, include_data_interface_properties=false, max_data_interface_properties=120, max_data_interface_property_value_length=512)`
  - Reads Data Interface module input override graph nodes, including linked input nodes, RenderTarget2D Data Interface User parameter bindings, and current User object defaults.
  - Reflected editable Data Interface property snapshots are omitted by default; pass `include_data_interface_properties=true` only when deep debugging needs them.
  - This is read-only and is intended for RenderTarget/Grid2D workflows where RapidIteration inspection cannot see object-valued Data Interface overrides.
- `create_niagara_module_input_override(system_path, input_name, value, emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", module_index=None, module_name="", module_node_guid="", overwrite_existing=false, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=false, timeout_seconds=10.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.1)`
  - Creates a missing RapidIteration module input override on an existing module input.
  - Scalar/vector/color/bool inputs retain their existing JSON forms. Enum-backed inputs accept an exact integer or an internal, authored, full, or display name string such as `ECC_WorldStatic`; hidden and terminal `MAX` entries are rejected. UE 5.6 can discard enum RapidIteration entries during compilation, so persisted enum authoring must use `set_niagara_module_input_literal_override` and verify the typed graph-pin default after compile.
  - Refuses source assets by default and refuses to overwrite an existing override unless `overwrite_existing=true` is passed.
- `set_niagara_module_static_switch(system_path, input_name="", value=None, emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", module_index=None, module_name="", module_node_guid="", expected_current_value="", allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=true, timeout_seconds=60.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.1, require_compile_gate_for_save=true)`
  - With no input/value, lists static switches and preserves the legacy internal-name `options` array while adding enum display/authored/numeric metadata, current-value validity, and hidden-state evidence.
  - Enum writes accept a display name, internal/full/authored name, or exact integer value, then validate against the pin's actual `UEnum`, reject Hidden/Spacer/MAX entries, and serialize the canonical internal pin value. Boolean switches accept booleans or `true`/`false` strings.
  - `expected_current_value` is an optional case-sensitive stale-write contract. The Python route requires an actual compile launch, a stable post-request Compile ID, final pin readback, and ready affected scripts whose cached and computed Compile IDs match before saving by default; a timeout or missing/non-ready/changed/unsynchronized compile evidence blocks the disk save and reports that the in-memory package remains dirty.
- `set_niagara_module_input_literal_override(system_path, input_name, value, emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", module_index=None, module_name="", module_node_guid="", overwrite_existing=false, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=false, timeout_seconds=10.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.1)`
  - Sets a scalar/vector/color/bool or enum module input through UE's typed override-pin `DefaultValue` string path. Enum values accept the same exact integer or internal/authored/full/display-name forms as RapidIteration conversion, including values such as `ECC_WorldStatic`.
  - This first-pass route is temp/generated scoped by default and is intended for non-RapidIteration literal module inputs after inspection.
  - It refuses existing linked override graphs instead of deleting them; `overwrite_existing=true` only replaces an existing unlinked default string.
- `set_niagara_render_target2d_module_input(system_path, input_name, user_parameter_name="User.RT_IF_Deform", render_target_asset_path="", emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", module_index=None, module_name="", module_node_guid="", inherit_user_parameter_settings=true, overwrite_existing=false, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=false, timeout_seconds=10.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.1)`
  - Creates a Niagara stack override for a RenderTarget2D Data Interface module input and binds it to a `UTextureRenderTarget2D` User parameter asset.
- `set_niagara_texture2d_module_input(system_path, input_name, user_parameter_name="User.T_Mask", texture_asset_path="", emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", module_index=None, module_name="", module_node_guid="", overwrite_existing=false, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=false, timeout_seconds=10.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.1)`
  - Creates a Niagara stack override for a Texture2D Data Interface module input and binds it to a `UTexture` User parameter backed by an optional `UTexture2D` default asset.
  - Use this for inputs such as `RenderGrid.Render Target 2D`; RapidIteration module-input tools cannot author Data Interface object inputs.
  - Refuses source assets by default and refuses to replace an existing linked override unless `overwrite_existing=true` is passed.
- `set_niagara_module_input_user_parameter(system_path, input_name, user_parameter_name, default_value=None, emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", module_index=None, module_name="", module_node_guid="", overwrite_existing=false, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=false, timeout_seconds=10.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.1)`
  - Creates a Niagara stack override for a scalar/vector/color/bool module input and links it to a matching `User.*` parameter.
  - Creates the User parameter when missing, rejects incompatible existing User parameter types, and can set an optional default value.
  - When overwriting, direct input nodes, parameter-map-get nodes, and single-output dynamic-input function nodes are supported; shared-output or unsupported graph shapes are refused.
  - Use this for runtime-driven source payload inputs such as UV, radius, strength, or color. Data Interface/object inputs still require dedicated commands.
- `set_niagara_array_data_interface_module_input_user_parameter(system_path, input_name, user_parameter_name, emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", module_index=None, module_name="", module_node_guid="", overwrite_existing=false, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=false, timeout_seconds=10.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.1)`
  - Creates a Niagara stack override for a supported Array Data Interface module input and links it to a matching `User.*` array parameter.
  - Supported inputs are Position Array, Float3 Array, Float2 Array, Float Array, and Int32 Array DIs.
  - Creates the User parameter and backing DI object when missing; it does not accept literal `default_value` because runtime array contents should be pushed from Blueprint with `Set Niagara Array Position/Vector/Float/Int`.
  - Use this as the module-input leg of the runtime array DI chain: `User parameter -> Module input -> Custom HLSL input`.
- `set_niagara_module_input_linked_parameter(system_path, input_name, linked_parameter_name, emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", module_index=None, module_name="", module_node_guid="", overwrite_existing=false, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=false, timeout_seconds=10.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.1)`
  - Links a Niagara module input to an existing namespaced parameter such as `Emitter.Grid2D Collection` or `User.MyParameter`.
- `set_niagara_module_inputs_batch(system_path, edits, operation="set_existing", overwrite_existing=false, continue_on_error=false, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=false, timeout_seconds=10.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.1)`
  - Applies multiple RapidIteration module input edits in one command and saves once after successful edits.
  - `operation` may be `set_existing`, `create_override`, or `upsert`; each edit object may override the operation and selectors.
- `set_niagara_module_input_value(system_path, input_name, value, emitter_index=None, emitter_name="", module_index=None, module_name="", module_node_guid="", allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true, wait_for_completion=false, timeout_seconds=10.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.1)`
  - Sets an existing RapidIteration module input override.
  - Does not create new RapidIteration overrides when no existing parameter data is present.
  - Module-input write commands return a `compile_wait` object; pass `wait_for_completion=true` to poll outstanding Niagara compilation before the command returns.
- `inspect_niagara_rapid_iteration_parameters(system_path, contains=None, max_parameters_per_script=256)`
  - Reads RapidIteration parameter names, types, values, script ownership, and control hints from a Niagara System.
  - Use this before exact-name edits because RapidIteration parameter names are generated and can be long.
- `set_niagara_rapid_iteration_parameter(system_path, parameter_name, value, owner_kind="", owner_name="", script_usage="", emitter_index=None, allow_source_edit=false, save=true, request_compile=true)`
  - Sets one existing RapidIteration parameter by exact name and optional script/owner filters.
  - Refuses source assets by default and does not create missing RapidIteration parameters.
  - If the exact name matches multiple scripts, the command returns the matches and requires `owner_kind`, `owner_name`, `script_usage`, or `emitter_index`.

## Safety Rules

- Default write scope is generated/temp Niagara work under `/Game/_MCP_Temp/NiagaraGenerated/`.
- Factory bootstrap inspection is transient-only and may be used on any editor session because it does not touch content packages.
- Niagara asset creation commands use UE factories plus `AssetTools.CreateAsset`, reject overwrite in the first pass, save with normal package semantics, and return dependency audit data.
- Prefer `cleanup_generated_niagara_assets_offline` for generated Niagara test asset cleanup after closing the editor. Avoid deleting freshly loaded Niagara Systems through live `EditorAssetLibrary.delete_asset` in D3D12 editor sessions.
- Preset creation failure cleanup is deferred rather than live-deleting the partially created Niagara System. Use the returned `created_asset_cleanup_path` with `cleanup_generated_niagara_assets_offline` after closing the editor.
- Keep source Niagara systems read-only unless the caller explicitly passes `allow_source_edit=true`.
- Prefer duplicating a source system first, then editing the duplicate.
- Treat unrestricted Scratch Pad internal graph wiring and emitter merging as future work. `inspect_niagara_graph_actions` now exposes the engine action catalog, but `apply_niagara_scratch_pad_graph_recipe` admits only allowlisted native node classes, exact hash-guarded Custom HLSL replacement, and generated ghost systems. Existing narrow ParameterMapSet and stock-module routes remain available separately.
- Emitter attach/duplicate writes are target-temp-system only by default through `duplicate_or_attach_emitter_from_source`.
- Scratch Pad duplication, stack insertion, narrow parameter-write graph mutation, the Vector2D User-parameter recipe, and the visible snow seed recipe are target-temp-system only by default through `create_or_duplicate_scratch_pad_module`, `add_scratch_pad_module_to_stack`, `add_niagara_scratch_pad_parameter_write`, `create_niagara_scratch_pad_vec2_user_parameter_module`, and `create_niagara_visible_scratch_pad_snow_seed`.
- Stock module stack insertion writes are target-temp-system only by default through `add_niagara_stock_module_to_stack`.
- Scratch Pad internal single-pin default edits are target-temp-system only by default through `set_niagara_scratch_pad_function_input_default`.
- Scratch Pad Custom HLSL dynamic inputs require a `Map` ParameterMap input when `requires_context=true`; otherwise Niagara's translator reports a dynamic-input signature error. `insert_niagara_scratch_pad_custom_hlsl_for_pin` auto-wires `Map` from the target ParameterMap source when the caller omits an explicit `Map` input. It defaults to `custom_hlsl_script_usage="DynamicInput"`; generated/temp diagnostics may pass `"Function"` when a reviewed probe needs statement-style Custom HLSL that assigns the named output pin.
- New RapidIteration override creation is available through `create_niagara_module_input_override`, guarded to generated/temp Niagara systems by default.
- Static enum/bool switches use `set_niagara_module_static_switch`; regular literal override-pin writing remains in `set_niagara_module_input_literal_override`, guarded to generated/temp Niagara systems by default and limited to unlinked scalar/vector/color/bool/enum inputs.
- RenderTarget2D and Texture2D Data Interface input binding is available through `set_niagara_render_target2d_module_input` and `set_niagara_texture2d_module_input`, guarded to generated/temp Niagara systems by default unless `allow_source_edit=true` is passed.
- Scalar/vector/color/bool module input User-parameter linking is available through `set_niagara_module_input_user_parameter`, guarded to generated/temp Niagara systems by default unless `allow_source_edit=true` is passed.
- Supported Array Data Interface module input User-parameter linking is available through `set_niagara_array_data_interface_module_input_user_parameter`; use it with `insert_niagara_scratch_pad_custom_hlsl_for_pin.user_parameter_inputs` or `rewire_niagara_custom_hlsl_input_to_module_parameter` to keep the runtime chain explicit.
- Compile-status inspection is read-only by default. Compile requests are allowed by default only under `/Game/_MCP_Temp/NiagaraGenerated/`.
- `replace_niagara_custom_hlsl` treats command dispatch, compile request, and compile completion as separate facts. Do not substitute `compile_requested=true` for `compile_effect_verified=true` in authoring gates.
- Niagara Script recompilation is limited to generated/temp Niagara content by default through `recompile_niagara_scripts_in_root`.
- Niagara Parameter Collection value edits are generated/temp-only by default through `set_niagara_parameter_collection_values`; `inspect_niagara_parameter_collection_values` is read-only.
- SimulationStage inspection is read-only and safe for source assets; it does not request compile, save, or mutate Niagara assets.
- Grid SimulationStage creation is generated/temp-system only by default through `add_niagara_grid_simulation_stage`; production promotion must pass `allow_source_edit=true` after review.
- SimulationStage removal is generated/temp-system only by default through `remove_niagara_simulation_stage`; production use must be explicitly reviewed.
- SimulationStage setting edits are generated/temp-system only by default through `set_niagara_simulation_stage_settings`; use `allow_source_edit=true` only after review.
- Data Interface override inspection is read-only and safe for source assets; it does not request compile, save, or mutate Niagara assets.
- Exact RapidIteration parameter edits are generated/temp-system only by default through `set_niagara_rapid_iteration_parameter`; inspect first and pass `allow_source_edit=true` only after review.

## Maintenance

From-scratch Niagara authoring research plan:

```text
Docs/Research/niagara_from_scratch_authoring_research_plan.md
```

From-scratch Niagara module-seed smoke:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\smoke_niagara_from_scratch_module_seed.py live --run-preview --allow-current-map-preview
```

This creates a generated temp basic sprite system, applies the MCPWeather snow particle material by default, inserts stock BoxLocation/force/noise/color/size modules, links selected module inputs to `User.*` parameters, checks compile/renderers/user parameters/promotion audit, and writes a report under `MCPGameProject/Saved/MCP/NiagaraReviews/<run_id>/from_scratch_module_seed_report.json`. Cleanup is offline-only after closing Unreal Editor:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\smoke_niagara_from_scratch_module_seed.py cleanup --name-prefix NS_MCP_FromScratch_ModuleSeed_<run_id> --delete
```

Scratch Pad graph-authoring smoke:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\smoke_niagara_scratch_pad_graph_authoring.py live
```

This creates a temp duplicate of `/Game/MCPWeather/FX/Snow/NS_MCPWeather_Snow`, locates the `Sample_Snow_Impact` Scratch Pad graph, runs the Scratch Pad graph admission preflight, inserts a Custom HLSL passthrough on `Particles.Position`, verifies the bridge auto-added the required context `Map` input alongside `BaseValue`, checks compile/renderers/graph readback/promotion audit, and writes a report under `MCPGameProject/Saved/MCP/NiagaraReviews/<run_id>/scratch_pad_graph_authoring_report.json`. Add `--run-preview --allow-current-map-preview` only when the editor has an active viewport for visual evidence; the core graph-authoring gate does not require preview. Cleanup is offline-only after closing Unreal Editor:

To regression-test the silent ChangeId failure class, add `--verify-consecutive-replacements`. The smoke replaces the same Custom HLSL node twice in one editor session and requires a fresh node ChangeId, dependent Compile ID invalidation, compile launch/completion, and compiled-data application on both writes:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\smoke_niagara_scratch_pad_graph_authoring.py live --verify-consecutive-replacements
```

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\smoke_niagara_scratch_pad_graph_authoring.py cleanup --name-prefix NS_MCP_ScratchPadGraphProof_<run_id> --delete
```

