Visible Scratch Pad recipe preview evidence:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\smoke_niagara_visible_scratch_pad_recipe.py live --run-preview --allow-current-map-preview
```

This extends the same smoke with `sample_niagara_system_in_preview_lab`, captures multiple warmup PNG frames, runs the bright-particle sparkle ratio gate, writes a contact sheet, and creates an MP4 when `ffmpeg` is available. The generated preview files live under `MCPGameProject/Saved/MCP/NiagaraReviews/<run_id>/visible_preview`; they are evidence artifacts, not Unreal assets.

Live validation `20260630_visible_scratch_pad_preview_v1` captured three frames, passed one sparkle-ratio frame, wrote a contact sheet and MP4, compiled `0/0`, and left no generated temp Niagara package after offline cleanup.

Visible Scratch Pad recipe promoted-temp release gate with UnrealMCP-disabled load:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\smoke_niagara_visible_scratch_pad_recipe.py live --run-preview --allow-current-map-preview --run-promoted-temp-release-gate --run-plugin-independence
```

This keeps both the source and promoted copy under `/Game/_MCP_Temp/NiagaraGenerated`, but exercises the real `plan_niagara_promotion_manifest` and `execute_niagara_promotion_manifest` confirmation-token flow. The promoted temp copy is rechecked for compile status, stock stack readback, User parameter readback, Scratch Pad graph readback, renderer material, promotion audit, and promoted preview evidence. `--run-plugin-independence` then runs the static forbidden-marker scan plus an isolated `UnrealEditor-Cmd.exe -DisablePlugins=UnrealMCP -EnablePlugins=PythonScriptPlugin` load against the promoted temp copy.

Live validation `20260630_visible_scratch_pad_promoted_temp_v2` passed the manifest dry-run, promoted one temp copy, revalidated source/promoted compile `0/0`, captured visible source/promoted MP4 evidence, passed the UnrealMCP-disabled isolated load, and left no generated temp Niagara package after offline cleanup.

Visible Scratch Pad recipe non-temp release candidate:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\smoke_niagara_visible_scratch_pad_recipe.py live --run-preview --allow-current-map-preview --run-non-temp-release-candidate --run-plugin-independence --release-target-system-path /Game/MCPWeather/Generated/NS_MCPWeather_VisibleScratchPadReleaseCandidate_<run_id>
```

This checks the requested `/Game/MCPWeather/Generated` target first with a read-only asset-exists preflight, then creates the temp visible Scratch Pad source, promotes it through the confirmation-token manifest flow with `allow_temp_target=false` and `allow_temp_dependencies=false`, saves the non-temp candidate, and revalidates the promoted asset for compile status, stock stack readback, User parameter readback, Scratch Pad graph readback, renderer material, exact Snow particle texture material, promotion audit, preview evidence, and UnrealMCP-disabled isolated load. The printed cleanup command only removes the generated temp source under `/Game/_MCP_Temp/NiagaraGenerated`; the non-temp candidate is project content and remains until intentionally deleted or versioned.

Live validation `20260630_visible_scratch_pad_non_temp_v1` created `/Game/MCPWeather/Generated/NS_MCPWeather_VisibleScratchPadReleaseCandidate_20260630_V1`, passed target preflight with `existing_target_count=0`, compiled source/release `0/0`, passed exact Snow particle material on one enabled Sprite renderer, captured three visible source frames and three visible release-candidate frames with MP4 evidence, passed static forbidden-marker scan, passed isolated `UnrealEditor-Cmd.exe -DisablePlugins=UnrealMCP` load with `loaded_asset_count=1`, and cleaned the temp source so the post-clean dry-run selected `0` packages.

Live validation `20260702_visible_scratch_pad_release_candidate_v2` created `/Game/MCPWeather/Generated/NS_MCPWeather_VisibleScratchPadReleaseCandidate_20260702_visible_scratch_pad_release_candidate_v2`, compiled source/release `0/0`, passed exact Snow particle material on one enabled Sprite renderer, captured `3/3` visible source frames and `3/3` visible release-candidate frames with MP4 evidence, passed static forbidden-marker scan, and passed isolated `UnrealEditor-Cmd.exe -DisablePlugins=UnrealMCP` load. The committed proof summary is `Docs/Analysis/MCPWeatherNiagara/visible_scratch_pad_release_candidate_20260702.json`.

