without the authoring bridge. It verifies no UnrealMCP bridge class or Python
symbols are available, then deletes only the exact temp package sidecars and
writes
`Docs/Analysis/MCPWeatherNiagara/niagara_bp_component_template_asset_swap_plugin_independence_canary_live_20260630.json`.
It does not admit durable original Blueprint mutation.

Generic Unreal asset plugin-independence gate:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\verify_unreal_asset_plugin_independence.py live --asset label=/Game/Path --expected-class label=/Script/Module.Class
```

This read-only verifier statically scans each requested `.uasset` for
UnrealMCP/MCP dependency markers, then loads the assets in
`UnrealEditor-Cmd.exe -DisablePlugins=UnrealMCP -EnablePlugins=PythonScriptPlugin`.
Unlike the MCPWeather release-candidate gate, it accepts arbitrary Unreal asset
classes such as Blueprint, Niagara System, Niagara Emitter, and Material. The
Reactive Niagara proof writes
`Docs/Analysis/ReactiveNiagara/reactive_assets_plugin_independence_20260702.json`.

Scratch Pad graph-shape contract:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\verify_niagara_scratch_pad_graph_shape_contract.py check
```

