Scratch Pad graph admission contract:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\niagara_scratch_pad_graph_admission_contract.py check
```

This read-only request matrix runs before live Scratch Pad graph authoring. The live Scratch Pad graph-authoring, blank parameter-write, blank User-parameter, color User-link, and visible Scratch Pad recipe smokes also record a `scratch_pad_graph_admission_preflight` stage before mutation. The contract admits the reviewed `Particles.SpriteSize` vec2 and `Particles.Color` Linear Color User-link shapes plus the guarded Custom HLSL passthrough with explicit `Map` context. It rejects arbitrary multi-node synthesis, overwrite/replace requests, direct non-temp graph writes, MCP-only dependency markers, Custom HLSL without context `Map`, and unknown parameter types. It writes `Docs/Analysis/MCPWeatherNiagara/niagara_scratch_pad_graph_admission_contract_20260630.json`.

For one planned request, run the evaluator before a live mutation:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\niagara_scratch_pad_graph_admission_contract.py evaluate --name planned_scratch_pad_edit --request-file .\request.json
```

By default `evaluate` exits non-zero when the request is rejected. Use `--expect rejected --fail-on unexpected` for negative tests.

