This creates the explicitly supplied Rain/Snow systems directly from empty target paths with `create_sprite_niagara_preset_system`. Direct project release-candidate mode intentionally has no fixed default target; every run must pass new empty `/Game/MCPWeather/Generated/...` paths through `--rain-release-target-system-path` and `--snow-release-target-system-path`. `--target-preflight-only` is read-only and does not overwrite the default direct-project evidence JSON unless `--analysis-output` is explicitly supplied. It does not promote, clone, duplicate, or create base temp sources. The gate preflights that targets do not exist, opts into `allow_non_temp_path`, verifies MCPWeather-owned materials/textures, compile/readback, preview visibility, static forbidden-marker scan, dependency audit, and UnrealMCP-disabled isolated load. The live report writes `Docs/Analysis/MCPWeatherNiagara/niagara_uds_style_weather_presets_direct_project_release_live_20260703.json`; project release candidates are not temp cleanup targets.

UDS-style direct-project target policy regression:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\test_niagara_uds_style_direct_project_policy.py
```

This offline regression test proves the direct project release route rejects missing Rain/Snow target arguments, temp paths, duplicate targets, and preflight-only default evidence overwrites before any live editor command is attempted.

Latest direct-project from-scratch validation:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\smoke_niagara_uds_style_weather_presets.py live --run-direct-project-release-candidate --run-preview --run-plugin-independence --allow-current-map-preview --run-id 20260703_niagara_uds_style_from_scratch_v4 --rain-release-target-system-path /Game/MCPWeather/Generated/NS_MCPWeather_UDSStyleFromScratch_Rain_20260703_V4 --snow-release-target-system-path /Game/MCPWeather/Generated/NS_MCPWeather_UDSStyleFromScratch_Snow_20260703_V4 --timeout-seconds 600 --plugin-independence-timeout-seconds 300
```

V4 creates both Rain and Snow from empty non-temp targets without source-template promotion or asset duplication. The default direct-project evidence JSON now records V4 as `created_from_scratch=true`, `uses_source_template=false`, `uses_asset_duplication=false`, preview-visible for both presets, compile `0/0`, clean dependency/static scans, and UnrealMCP-disabled isolated load pass. Future reruns must use new empty target paths or an explicit cleanup/replacement decision.

UDS-style texture-connection offline verifier:

