uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\verify_niagara_uds_style_texture_connections_offline.py check
```

This read-only verifier reconciles the V4 direct-project live report with static `.uasset` scans. It proves each generated Niagara system uses its MCPWeather-local particle material and each material references the expected local particle-sheet texture (`Rain/Textures/T_MCPWeather_RainSnow_Sheet` and `Snow/Textures/T_MCPWeather_RainSnow_Sheet`), while also checking preview visibility, compile `0/0`, dependency policy, plugin independence, and forbidden UnrealMCP/UDS runtime markers. It writes `Docs/Analysis/MCPWeatherNiagara/niagara_uds_style_weather_presets_texture_connections_20260703.json`.

Repeatable MCPWeather source-template smoke:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\smoke_niagara_mcpweather_source_template.py live --json
```

This defaults to the public Python `create_niagara_system_from_source_template` orchestration path, runs `audit_niagara_promotion_candidate`, dry-runs a non-temp promotion plan through `plan_niagara_promotion_manifest`, then creates a guarded promoted copy under the generated temp root through `execute_niagara_promotion_manifest` so the confirmed execution path is tested without leaving permanent content. Use `--route manual` only when testing the lower-level bridge sequence directly.

Offline promotion-manifest behavior smoke:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\test_niagara_promotion_manifest_flow.py
```

This fake-bridge test writes a temporary Saved/MCP manifest JSON, verifies bad confirmation tokens perform no command calls, reloads the manifest through `manifest_path`, executes a two-entry batch against a fake bridge, writes an execution report, and deletes both JSON files. Planning, revalidation, and apply all use the same strict promotion response validator. Execution reports distinguish attempted dispatches from confirmed promotions, preserve requested and observed recovery targets after an indeterminate apply, and retain confirmed mutation results even if execution-report I/O itself fails.

Promotion lifecycle boundary contract:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\niagara_promotion_lifecycle_boundary_contract.py check
```

This read-only contract verifies the current promotion boundary across Python wrapper defaults, manifest revalidation behavior, C++ overwrite refusal, docs, and the capability matrix. Promotion remains dry-run-first, explicit-target, confirmation-token gated, revalidated before mutation, and no-overwrite by default. Bulk promotion, overwrite/update, redirector-aware replacement, and lifecycle migration remain research-only until a separate lifecycle design is reviewed. The current default output is `Docs/Analysis/MCPWeatherNiagara/niagara_promotion_lifecycle_boundary_contract_20260702.json`; the earlier `20260630` report remains historical evidence.

Promotion overwrite/update preflight contract:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\niagara_promotion_overwrite_update_preflight_contract.py check
```

This read-only contract verifies that overwrite/update remains closed after the first promotion lifecycle review. Current promotion may still only duplicate to a new target after dry-run planning, confirmation-token execution, and revalidation. Before overwrite/update can be opened, a separate reviewed gate must add backup/restore proof, an explicit redirector/fixup policy, post-write dependency audit, execution reporting, and a plugin-independence check. The current default output is `Docs/Analysis/MCPWeatherNiagara/niagara_promotion_overwrite_update_preflight_contract_20260703.json`.

MCPWeather non-temp promotion path:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\promote_niagara_mcpweather_source_template.py live --json
```

This checks the requested promotion targets first with a read-only asset-exists preflight, then creates generated temp source-template systems, writes a promotion manifest for `/Game/MCPWeather/Generated/NS_MCPWeather_Generated_Rain` and `..._Snow`, and validates `all_can_promote` without writing non-temp assets. Use `--rain-target-system-path` and `--snow-target-system-path` when planning a new non-overwriting release candidate path, and use `--target-preflight-only` to check those target paths without creating temp assets. Add `--execute` only when intentionally creating those project content assets. Add `--run-release-gate` with `--execute` to immediately run the strict MCPWeather release gate against the promoted target paths; by default this includes preview, visual regression, and UnrealMCP plugin-independence checks. Rain release preview defaults to 6 frames and 480 promoted settle frames because shorter captures can under-sample visible rain despite healthy runtime particle counts. After the live run closes Unreal Editor, use the printed cleanup command to remove temp source systems.

MCPWeather split release gate:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\run_mcpweather_niagara_split_release_gate.py live --run-id 20260630_release_candidate_split_strict_v1 --rain-system-path /Game/MCPWeather/Generated/NS_MCPWeather_ReleaseCandidate_20260630_Rain --snow-system-path /Game/MCPWeather/Generated/NS_MCPWeather_ReleaseCandidate_20260630_Snow --run-visual-regression --run-plugin-independence --preset-retries 1
```

This runs the standard release gate once per preset, then writes one aggregate `split_release_gate_report.json` under `MCPGameProject/Saved/MCP/NiagaraReviews/<run_id>/`. It is the preferred validation path when a long-lived editor session can time out during the combined Rain/Snow preview. Visual regression stays per-preset so partial runs remain valid, and UnrealMCP plugin independence is run once for the selected asset set instead of once per preset. Use `--preset-retries 1` for release candidates so a single transient preview bridge timeout can retry the failed preset and record both attempts. The standard release gate also checks Snow sprite renderers for `/Game/MCPWeather/FX/Snow/Materials/M_MCPWeather_Snow_Particle`, so a Snow candidate with missing particle texture material fails before preview approval. When `texture_materials` is present in a release-gate report, `check_mcpweather_niagara_visual_regression.py` includes that material contract in the offline check list.

MCPWeather release-candidate evidence review:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\review_mcpweather_release_candidate_evidence.py check
```

This is an offline reconciliation step for the current Rain/Snow release-candidate evidence. It does not connect to Unreal Editor or touch project content. By default it reviews the Rain long strict report, Snow split retry report, Snow texture material gate report, current visual baseline, plugin-independence reports, and cleanup dry-run reports, then writes `Docs/Analysis/MCPWeatherNiagara/mcpweather_release_candidate_20260630_review.json`. Use this after preview sessions to regenerate a single pass/fail candidate evidence report without rerunning Niagara viewport captures. Cleanup state is reported under `maintenance.cleanup`; pending temp cleanup is not treated as a release-content failure.

Current MCPWeather release-candidate cleanup after closing Unreal Editor:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\promote_niagara_mcpweather_source_template.py cleanup --name-prefix NS_MCPWeatherPromotion_20260630_promotion_release_gate_contract_no_execute_ --delete
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\promote_niagara_mcpweather_source_template.py cleanup --name-prefix NS_MCPWeatherPromotion_20260630_release_candidate_execute_v1_ --delete
```

Dry-run evidence is stored under `Docs/Analysis/MCPWeatherNiagara/mcpweather_temp_cleanup_*_dry_run.json`. Each prefix selected two generated temp Niagara packages. Do not run the `--delete` commands while Unreal Editor is open.

One-command finalize wrapper:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\finalize_mcpweather_release_candidate_after_editor_close.py run
```

This runs the offline evidence review and cleanup dry-run together, writing `Docs/Analysis/MCPWeatherNiagara/mcpweather_release_candidate_finalize_20260630.json`. After closing Unreal Editor, add `--delete-cleanup` to delete the selected temp packages and then dry-run verify that no matching packages remain. The delete path still refuses to run while `UnrealEditor.exe` is active.

