Docs/Analysis/MCPWeatherNiagara/mcpweather_release_candidate_20260630_runbook.md
```

Use the runbook as the compact handoff for the current Rain/Snow release candidates, including evidence paths, editor-open cleanup restrictions, Snow texture-material contract, UnrealMCP plugin-independence contract, and the preferred split strict gate to rerun after an editor restart.

Current release-candidate status summary:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\mcpweather_release_candidate_status.py check
```

This read-only helper loads the current review/finalize JSON, verifies the runbook contract and candidate `.uasset` files, runs a fast forbidden-marker byte scan for `/Script/UnrealMCP`, `/UnrealMCP`, `UnrealMCP`, `MCPUnreal`, and `mcp_unreal`, probes the current `UnrealEditor.exe` process, then prints release status, cleanup-pending state, delete readiness, and next commands. Cleanup pending is treated as maintenance by default; add `--require-cleanup-complete` when the cleanup step must already be finished, or `--require-delete-ready` when the temp cleanup delete step is next and the editor must already be closed.

